@meta
id: 04-09
title: A count on an insert command
chapter: 04
type: lesson
skills: count-prefix
par: 40
minutes: 5
vscode: type the line, copy it, paste it five times
open: orders.fixture.csv

@brief
The count is not only for motions. Put one in front of a command that
inserts text and the whole insertion repeats, text and all, when you press
`Esc`.

    3ohello<Esc>

opens three new lines, each containing `hello`. One `o`, one count, one
piece of typing.

The load test needs padding rows in this fixture. Add six identical rows
to the end of the file, each exactly:

    ORD-0000,CUS-000,0,PENDING

Type that row once. The count does the other five.

@keys
| `6o` | open six new lines below and repeat what you type on each |
| `3O` | the same, opening above |
| `20i-` `Esc` | insert twenty hyphens |
| `5j` | down five lines |

@hints
Get to the last line of the file first. The new rows go below it.
--
The count goes in front of `o`, not after it, and the repetition happens
at the moment you press `Esc` — so the text only appears five more times
when you leave insert mode. That is normal; do not panic and retype it.
--
`5j`, then `6o`, type the row once, then `Esc`.

@solution
    5j 6o ORD-0000,CUS-000,0,PENDING <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Thirty-six keystrokes, twenty-six of which are the row itself. Without
the count it would have been the row six times: over a hundred and fifty
keystrokes, and a real chance of a typo in one of them that you would
find later, in a failing test, with no idea why.

This is the first time in the course that a count has done something
other than move you, and it is worth pausing on. `3o`, `5a`, `20i` and
`4A` all work this way: the command runs, you type, and `Esc` replays the
insertion the remaining times. It is the cheapest way to produce
repetitive text in vim, and in chapter 11 the `.` command will generalise
it to *any* edit, not just insertions.

One caution. The repeat is of the typing, exactly as typed. If you use
backspace or arrow keys while inserting, what gets repeated can surprise
you. Type the line clean, or undo and start again.

@start orders.fixture.csv
order_id,customer_id,total,status
ORD-2001,CUS-301,1999,PAID
ORD-2002,CUS-302,4750,PAID
ORD-2003,CUS-303,899,PENDING
ORD-2004,CUS-304,12500,PAID
ORD-2005,CUS-305,2399,SHIPPED

@expected orders.fixture.csv
order_id,customer_id,total,status
ORD-2001,CUS-301,1999,PAID
ORD-2002,CUS-302,4750,PAID
ORD-2003,CUS-303,899,PENDING
ORD-2004,CUS-304,12500,PAID
ORD-2005,CUS-305,2399,SHIPPED
ORD-0000,CUS-000,0,PENDING
ORD-0000,CUS-000,0,PENDING
ORD-0000,CUS-000,0,PENDING
ORD-0000,CUS-000,0,PENDING
ORD-0000,CUS-000,0,PENDING
ORD-0000,CUS-000,0,PENDING
